  "long18_low_occlusion": "Near to far. Tree obscures most of lower windows 1 and 2, the white garden wall crops several sills, and the farthest bays retain no readable subdivision. Labels count from camera in the image, not street numbers.",
  "certainty": "end18 edge picks usually ±1–2 px, street13 ±3–5 px for exterior reveals; long18 ±2 px for clear near edges and ±3–6 px at tree and distant silhouettes. Preserve the two sides of a vertical frame in their own image.",
  "profiles": {
    "narrow_sash": "One undivided segmental headlight over two tall leaves. Within each leaf two narrow horizontal glazing bars define three panes. The outer frame, intermediate transom, broad meeting stile and fine glazing bars have visibly different widths.",
    "wide_door": "Two leaves, each with three panes. Frame and intermediate rails visibly heavier than the narrow windows. One shallow upper light. Two vertical paired pulls on opposite sides of the meeting stile are visible in end18 on each of the two doors.",
    "finish": "Black-brown frames; dull metal door pulls. Some upper windows return the pale sky and apartment walls; the very dark door glazing returns the courtyard paving. Reflection and distant building edges are not new window mullions."
  }
}
